# Binaries. ANCHORED (leading /) on purpose: the bare patterns `mcp` and `cli`
# matched every directory of those names anywhere in the tree, including
# vendor/github.com/modelcontextprotocol/go-sdk/mcp - so 23 files of the MCP
# SDK's core package were silently never committed and a fresh clone could not
# build (`go build -mod=vendor ./...` -> "cannot find module providing package
# .../go-sdk/mcp"). The working tree built fine, because go mod vendor had put
# the files there locally.
/caido-mcp-server
Caido-CLI/caido
dist/
*.exe

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/

# Token
~/.caido-mcp/
.claude/

/mcp
/cli
